    "tips": [
      "Before asking Claude to draft anything, paste in the brief, previous examples, or relevant background. Claude writes to what it knows \u2014 without it, the output is generic.",
      "Be specific about the output format: \"A 200-word email in a direct, professional tone\" gets a better first draft than \"write an email about this\".",
      "If you are asking Claude to do something strategic \u2014 analyse options, review a proposal, assess a brief \u2014 tell it your role and who the audience is first.",
      "For recurring tasks, set up a Claude Project with a description of the client, their tone, and their constraints. Every conversation in that project then starts with that context already loaded."
